# Strumming: Steady Quarters (repertoire plan: st-strum-quarters). Your part: Em (022000) for
# 4 bars, A (x02220) for 4, then the same again: 16 bars of four even downstrums, a little
# stronger on beat 1, to the very last beat (the plan: downstrums on every beat, never stopping).
# SixTab cannot put an accent on a slash, so the stronger beat 1 is a note on the score.
# Start at 60 and raise the tempo in steps of 4.
# The teacher plays an original tune over the chords (E minor with an A major chord: the Dorian
# colour, C#). Its notes on beats 1 and 3 are always notes of the chord in force.
title: Strumming: Steady Quarters
id: st-strum-quarters
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original strumming study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 1
tags: strumming, downstrums, quarter notes, beginner
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: E Dorian

track: Your strum
role: rhythm
[First time]
strum: DDDD
| ^"beat 1 a little stronger" "Em=022000" q D D D D | D D D D | D D D D | D D D D |
| "A=x02220" D D D D | D D D D | D D D D | D D D D |
[Second time]
strum: DDDD
| "Em=022000" D D D D | D D D D | D D D D | D D D D |
| "A=x02220" D D D D | D D D D | D D D D | D D D D ||

track: Teacher
role: lead
[First time]
| h 2:0 q 3:0 2:0 | h 1:0 2:0 | q 3:0 3:2 h 2:0 | q 2:0 3:2 h 3:0 |
| h 2:2 q 3:2 2:2 | h 1:0 2:2 | q 3:2 2:0 h 2:2 | q 2:2 2:0 h 3:2 |
[Second time]
| h 2:0 q 3:0 2:0 | q 1:0 1:2 h 1:3 | q 1:0 2:3 h 2:0 | q 3:0 3:2 h 2:0 |
| h 2:2 q 1:0 2:2 | h 3:2 2:2 | q 3:2 2:0 h 2:2 | w 1:0 ||
